# Files the repair tool must not touch.
#
# Trunk Check lints the files a change touches and reports their EXISTING
# findings as new ones. A file with a pre-existing mypy error or a dead import
# fails the gate the moment anything modifies it, even a one-line path fix.
# Those files need their own cleanup, not a path rewrite bolted onto it.
#
#   scripts/e2e_real_model.py                    mypy name-defined: "mx"
#   gui/admin-extensions/api/research_panel.py   2 mypy failures
#   scripts/phenotype_omlx_ready.py              ruff F401, unused imports
#
# beads/bead-ctl.sh is excluded for a different reason. Making it shfmt-clean
# moves a line whose comment says the dual write is switched off, and rule R7 of
# the happy-path guard has no escape hatch at all: any added line mentioning a
# disabled feature is reported. Fixing R7 is a change to the rule itself and
# belongs in its own commit.
#
# The twelve shell files that used to be listed here are no longer excluded.
# They were blocked by the guard reading the shell loop terminator, and a word
# inside a quoted string, as unverified success claims. That was a false
# positive in the guard's rule R1, corrected in governance/happy-path-precommit.sh
# with tests in governance/test-happy-path-claims.sh.

scripts/e2e_real_model.py
gui/admin-extensions/api/research_panel.py
scripts/phenotype_omlx_ready.py
beads/bead-ctl.sh
